#DESCRIPTION
Free-stream (uniform-equilibrium) regression test of the HYBRID field solver
(generalized Ohm's law + Faraday) with the Hall term OFF: solveEM=F,
useHybridPIC=T, useHallTerm=F.

The initial condition is a uniform plasma with 1 kinetic ion species (electrons
are an implicit neutralizing fluid), uniform bulk flow ux = 100 km/s (Mach 1, Alfven speed),
a 3D oblique magnetic field (Bx, By, Bz), plasma beta ~ 1 (T = 314000 K), and the
corresponding convective electric field E = -u x B.  Shares the identical grid,
plasma, normalization, timestepping, and output with PARAM.in (full PIC),
differing only in the field-solver block.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
32                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

Standard Maxwell/GMRES solver disabled; use the Ohm's-law + Faraday hybrid
field advance instead.
#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

#HALLTERM
F                       useHallTerm

#RESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
0.0                     electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

#BSUBCYCLE
1                       nBSubcycle

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nS
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
100.0                   ux [km/s]      fast bulk flow (U_code = 1.0 = v_A)
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
314000.0                T [K]          beta ~ 1 (T_code ~ 0.26)
8.0e-9                  bx [T]         3D oblique magnetic field (|B| ~ 10.44 nT)
6.0e-9                  by [T]
3.0e-9                  bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]       convective electric field E = -u x B
3.0e-4                  ey [V/m]       Ey = ux * Bz
-6.0e-4                 ez [V/m]       Ez = -ux * By

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s] tNorm = 1 s; sets cLight_SI = uNormSI

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
2000                    npcelx
1                       npcely
1                       npcelz

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn
10.0                    dt
1                       dx
Bx By Bz Ex Ey Ez       varName

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
10.0                    TimeMax   ~1.6 ion gyroperiods (stability)

#RUN
